+Feature: Methodology Conformance
+  Shipshape methodology checks that verify the project's own method,
+  in contrast to the product. These scenarios are tagged conformance -
+  they are skeletons derived from code inspection, non-binding until
+  Captain promotes them.
+
+  @captain
+  @conformance
+  Scenario: Watchbill shape conforms to specification
+    Given the project root directory
+    When I scan for a watchbill.json file
+    Then the file, if present, contains only ordered watch objects named "watch1", "watch2", and onward
+    And each watch object contains only a "scenarios" array of scenario references or tier tags
+
+  @captain
+  @conformance
+  Scenario: No PERTURBATION token stands in implementation code
+    Given the implementation directories "js" and "index.html"
+    When I search for the literal "PERTURBATION" token in the implementation files
+    Then no matches are found in the implementation files
\ No newline at end of file
